        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8eaaecbe-eaeb-568e-947f-dab344194b8e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lewis Cunningham Broadus\n- Roles: Buffalo Soldier, Captain\n- Organizations: United States Army\n- Military Units: 25th Infantry Regiment, 92nd Infantry Division\n- Places: Henrico County, Virginia, Mexico-United States border region, North America\n- Events: Border War, Border Campaign, Mexican Revolution\n\nFacts:\n- Lewis Cunningham Broadus was born in 1877 in Henrico County, Virginia.\n- The Border War, also called the Border Campaign, refers to military engagements in the Mexico-United States border region of North America during the Mexican Revolution from 1910 to 1919.\n- Lewis Cunningham Broadus served with distinction as a Buffalo Soldier in the 25th Infantry Regiment and the 92nd Infantry Division of the United States Army.\n- Lewis Cunningham Broadus died in 1961.",
